{
  "key": "jordan",
  "version": 2,
  "name_ar": "دليل حسابات للمملكة الأردنية الهاشمية",
  "name_en": "Jordan chart of accounts",
  "countries": [
    "JO"
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "IFRS as required by the Companies Law, with the statutory accounts a Jordanian entity needs for general sales tax, income tax, the national contribution and social security",
    "url": "https://www.istd.gov.jo/",
    "note": "No national chart of accounts is mandated for private companies in Jordan either, and this template claims none. Its structure is the generic IFRS one - the Companies Law requires audited statements under internationally recognised standards - and what it adds is what a Jordanian entity is obliged to account for separately: general sales tax administered by the Income and Sales Tax Department, income tax under the Income Tax Law, the national contribution that certain sectors bear in addition to it, tax withheld at source, and Social Security Corporation contributions. The GST accounts carry the SAME control roles as the VAT accounts in the other templates, which is the point of a role: the tax has a different name and a different rate in each jurisdiction, and the posting rules do not change. No rate appears here; rates belong to the tax engine, where a change is dated."
  },
